// imgIn, imgOut, y1, y2: i x j
//
// Optimized version:
//
// - Precomputes exponentials/powers once and reuses them for all coefficients.
// - Keeps the 1D IIR recurrences strictly along j (vertical passes) or i
//   (horizontal passes) to preserve Deriche filter semantics.
// - Fuses the vertical anti-causal pass with the vertical combine, so we never
//   materialize a full vertical y2 image.
// - Fuses the horizontal anti-causal pass with the final combine, so we never
//   materialize a full horizontal y2 image either.
// - Uses Noarr traversers everywhere to express loop nests.
//
[[gnu::flatten, gnu::noinline]]
void kernel_deriche(num_t alpha, auto imgIn, auto imgOut, auto y1, auto y2) {
